# Hand-authored architecture map -> d2 -> svg via `sh`.
#
# Proof-of-capability: the trait/type interaction graph is supplied as
# hand-made facts (no resolver needed yet). sprf maintains them, projects
# to d2 source, writes the .d2, and shells out to `d2` to render the svg.
#
# Run from repo root:
#   cargo run --manifest-path v4/Cargo.toml --bin sprefa-run -- \
#     v4/examples/arch-d2-map.sprf --root . --show-rows

rule(:arch_node, ID?, LABEL?);
rule(:arch_edge, SRC?, DST?, REL?);

# --- hand-made node facts: the main traits/types ---
`OperatorDef|compile-time op trait. lower is the compile to runtime bridge
Component|runtime op trait. render render_batch dispatch tiers
Node|op output algebra. Emit Many Park Done
RenderCtx|dispatch context. pipe hash depth generation bus diagnostics
Cursor|payload. focal term plus named terms
FactRuntimeGraph|reactive state graph. subscribe support dirty sweep
RuntimeGraph|v4 facade over FactRuntimeGraph
owner_uri|owner identity key. fiber or switchMap key
Subscribe|source in-edge. owner consumes source
support|owner keyed-children keep-alive set. DAG reconcile by key`
  > split`
`
  > re`(?P<ID>[^|]+)\|(?P<LABEL>.+)`
  > arch_node(ID, LABEL);

# --- hand-made edge facts: how they interact ---
`OperatorDef|Component|lower bridges compile to runtime
Component|Node|render / dispatch return value
Component|RenderCtx|dispatch reads ctx
Cursor|Component|batch input
RuntimeGraph|FactRuntimeGraph|delegates all state
Subscribe|FactRuntimeGraph|inserts the subscribe edge
owner_uri|RuntimeGraph|keys owner instances
support|FactRuntimeGraph|refcount keep-alive set
FactRuntimeGraph|Node|dirty sweep re-runs owners`
  > split`
`
  > re`(?P<SRC>[^|]+)\|(?P<DST>[^|]+)\|(?P<REL>.+)`
  > arch_edge(SRC, DST, REL);

# --- project facts -> d2 source, write, then render via sh ---
`arch-map`
  > render.markdown`direction: right

${ arch_node?(ID?, LABEL?)
  > render.markdown`n_${ID}: ${LABEL}
`
}
${ arch_edge?(SRC?, DST?, REL?)
  > render.markdown`n_${SRC} -> n_${DST}: ${REL}
`
}
`
  > write_file`v4/examples/arch-map.d2`
  > sh`d2 v4/examples/arch-map.d2 v4/examples/arch-map.svg && echo d2-rendered`;
